WEBVTT

00:51.051 --> 00:52.927
Let's forget this.

00:53.011 --> 00:54.679
No drama. Like adults.

00:54.763 --> 00:56.639
I hope things stay normal.

00:56.723 --> 00:59.476
No drama. Like adults.

01:00.977 --> 01:03.063
So…

01:27.378 --> 01:29.089
I've gone insane.

01:34.677 --> 01:36.137
Are you hungry?

01:36.221 --> 01:37.972
Do you wanna grab something to… Oh!

01:56.825 --> 01:58.326
Ha-kyung's still not home?

01:59.536 --> 02:02.997
And what did she say
yesterday on the phone?

02:03.081 --> 02:07.043
She said, uh, don't you worry
'cause she will fight Han Ki-jun and win.

02:18.930 --> 02:20.390
Hey! You…

02:20.473 --> 02:22.809
How about you give us a call
if you're not coming home?

02:22.892 --> 02:24.394
You know how worried Mom was?

02:25.937 --> 02:27.856
Where were you? Coming back from work?

02:29.149 --> 02:30.150
Uh-huh.

02:31.025 --> 02:33.111
- Breakfast?
- I'm not hungry.

02:39.409 --> 02:41.035
She's not thinking about eating.

02:41.119 --> 02:42.704
I know the look on her face.

02:43.580 --> 02:45.248
It's a problem with closure.

02:46.291 --> 02:48.459
I know at heart she's a smart person.

02:48.543 --> 02:49.836
Only sometimes it feels like

02:49.919 --> 02:52.630
she can't take what she's owed
in life from anyone.

02:55.049 --> 02:56.217
Wait a second.

03:18.656 --> 03:21.075
- Oh, no.
- She's crying?

03:22.619 --> 03:24.537
- Out of my way.
- Oh, no, Mom. Ma.

03:25.121 --> 03:26.456
Let her be.

03:26.539 --> 03:27.665
You get it?

03:27.749 --> 03:30.919
She got a hole shot through her heart
from the dude that she was going to marry.

03:31.002 --> 03:33.755
That guy, that guy,
I knew he was a problem.

03:33.838 --> 03:35.632
The way she always made excuses.

03:35.715 --> 03:38.551
Yes, I know. And I'm sure
she's embarrassed right now.

03:38.635 --> 03:41.721
What's she embarrassed for, huh?
It fell apart because he wronged her.

03:41.804 --> 03:44.682
Mom, let's let her rest, huh?

03:44.766 --> 03:48.394
Let's just go and give her a chance
to think it through, huh?

04:12.669 --> 04:13.753
I'm insane.

04:27.392 --> 04:30.270
The yellow dust affecting air conditions
last night is gone.

04:30.353 --> 04:34.607
Overall, it will feel a little more
like early summer than a spring day today.

04:34.691 --> 04:38.361
Midday temperatures are set to reach
up to 28 degrees in Seoul.

04:38.444 --> 04:41.030
Eight degrees higher than yesterday.

04:48.663 --> 04:50.498
It's tough
when the season's changing.

04:53.293 --> 04:57.171
You don't know whether to wear
thick layers or thin.

04:58.715 --> 05:00.091
TRY A SUMMER DELICACY!

05:00.174 --> 05:01.718
- Bye. Thank you.
- Thank you.

05:01.801 --> 05:03.594
COLD BUCKWHEAT NOODLES
SPICY BUCKWHEAT NOODLES

05:05.305 --> 05:08.766
- Eat hot food or cold.
- Yes. Mm-hmm.

05:09.559 --> 05:10.852
- Hello.
- Hello.

05:16.149 --> 05:17.775
Uh, hot, uh…

05:17.859 --> 05:19.694
Uh, no, uh, iced Americano, please.

05:19.777 --> 05:21.029
- Just one?
- Yeah.

05:21.112 --> 05:22.572
- Okay.
- Thank you.

05:33.374 --> 05:38.212
That's why sometimes I can't tell
if this feeling I'm feeling

05:38.296 --> 05:41.007
is sorrow for the season
I'm leaving behind

05:41.090 --> 05:45.011
or excitement for the season soon to come.

05:45.762 --> 05:47.680
Please walk.

05:50.933 --> 05:54.520
But one thing's for sure.
Summer's almost here.

06:25.468 --> 06:31.099
EPISODE 3
IN BETWEEN SEASONS

07:10.513 --> 07:13.683
Leaving for work.
I made breakfast. Eat before you leave.

07:27.738 --> 07:28.739
Hmm?

07:40.543 --> 07:42.587
Oh, off to school?

07:44.422 --> 07:45.840
See you later.

07:45.923 --> 07:48.176
Call me
when your afterschool classes are over.

07:48.259 --> 07:49.594
- Okay.
- Ah, have a good day.

07:53.139 --> 07:55.850
What's with her?
Is she always sour in the morning?

07:55.933 --> 07:59.395
You can't just walk around like that
in front of your grownup daughter.

08:00.438 --> 08:01.481
Oh…

08:01.564 --> 08:03.816
Why? I am her father.

08:04.692 --> 08:09.822
Yeah. I suppose so, but she hasn't lived
with you for over 14 years.

08:17.872 --> 08:19.123
Breakfast is ready.

08:19.207 --> 08:20.458
At least have a little, huh?

08:20.541 --> 08:21.501
I'm late.

08:25.254 --> 08:28.883
Your car isn't out front.
Where is it, at work or uh…

08:33.012 --> 08:34.514
Oh!

08:42.438 --> 08:44.774
Ah, it's fine.

08:44.857 --> 08:45.691
See you later.

08:47.443 --> 08:49.737
My gosh, this is insane.

08:51.656 --> 08:52.782
Yes.

08:54.492 --> 08:57.328
No. We didn't find any car keys anywhere.

08:57.912 --> 08:58.829
Really?

08:58.913 --> 09:01.207
Can you check one more time?
'Cause I wanna be really sure.

09:01.290 --> 09:02.833
Yes. Thank you.

09:10.508 --> 09:11.759
Oh, yes.

09:12.927 --> 09:15.638
Um, the last seven days of buoy report.

09:15.721 --> 09:17.890
BUOY: EQUIPMENT USED
TO OBSERVE WEATHER CONDITIONS AT SEA

09:17.974 --> 09:20.434
Oh, they were in already.
Well, okay, thanks.

09:28.901 --> 09:31.237
- Sounds like you've got a cold.
- Yeah.

09:31.320 --> 09:33.531
Mm-hmm. You should be careful.

09:34.282 --> 09:35.950
Did you sleep in the cold?

09:37.034 --> 09:38.035
No.

09:48.254 --> 09:49.964
No.

09:50.965 --> 09:53.301
Did you… stay out last night?

09:53.384 --> 09:54.594
You wore that yesterday.

09:57.430 --> 09:58.973
You didn't go home?

10:00.850 --> 10:02.351
That's not important.

10:02.435 --> 10:05.021
Ooh, how intriguing,
Forecaster.

10:05.104 --> 10:06.689
You're a fascinating guy.

10:06.772 --> 10:08.649
Ooh…

10:08.733 --> 10:09.984
It's not that.

10:10.067 --> 10:12.069
I haven't found a new home,
so I've been staying over

10:12.153 --> 10:13.654
at the new training center.

10:13.738 --> 10:16.699
But, uh, I have to be out of there
before the month's over.

10:16.782 --> 10:18.326
So my stuff's all sealed up.

10:18.993 --> 10:20.369
I see.

10:20.453 --> 10:23.205
Oh, Shin, don't you have a spare room?

10:23.789 --> 10:26.000
Didn't you win
an apartment voucher last year?

10:27.835 --> 10:28.669
Did you?

10:29.545 --> 10:31.672
It's not mine, really. It's the bank's.

10:31.756 --> 10:34.717
Hey, I'm not asking to stay for free.
I'd pay fair rent.

10:34.800 --> 10:37.345
Si-woo, I'm not the type
who can live with another person.

10:38.846 --> 10:41.724
Where is Director Jin?
Is she always this late?

10:43.934 --> 10:45.394
CHIEF TEAM TWO, DIRECTOR JIN HA-KYUNG

10:48.981 --> 10:50.191
That's strange.

10:50.274 --> 10:51.901
She's never been late before.

11:21.555 --> 11:23.933
Director, where are you?
We're starting the meeting.

11:24.892 --> 11:26.394
There's a lot of traffic.

11:27.978 --> 11:30.690
Let Senior Forecaster Um open the meeting.

11:41.450 --> 11:43.244
Director Jin is running a little late.

11:43.327 --> 11:45.413
She said you should open
the meeting and start it.

11:49.166 --> 11:50.334
All right. Good morning.

11:51.001 --> 11:53.003
All right, all right. Hey.

12:05.391 --> 12:07.435
KMA BUS STOP

12:22.867 --> 12:24.118
You're all right. Sit.

12:25.536 --> 12:28.247
- Has it started?
- She's not even here yet.

12:28.330 --> 12:29.498
She's not here?

12:32.668 --> 12:35.129
Soo-jin, did you tell him?

13:02.740 --> 13:04.033
Where is Director Jin?

13:04.784 --> 13:07.036
She's not
even reading my messages anymore.

13:09.914 --> 13:12.082
Ask Senior Forecaster Um
to start the meeting.

13:12.166 --> 13:14.335
I told him twice already.

13:16.212 --> 13:17.671
But he isn't doing anything.

13:21.383 --> 13:23.886
Senior Forecaster Um,
you should start the meeting.

13:27.723 --> 13:28.933
Mr. Um.

13:47.409 --> 13:50.329
I'm sorry.

13:50.412 --> 13:52.289
I left my car here last night…

13:52.373 --> 13:54.416
Okay, whatever. Let's get started.

13:54.500 --> 13:55.626
I'm sorry.

14:07.221 --> 14:08.222
I'm sorry.

14:19.942 --> 14:20.901
Can we start?

14:21.569 --> 14:22.653
Yes.

14:27.199 --> 14:29.618
We will now call to order
our meeting for May 10th.

14:29.702 --> 14:32.246
Okay, satellite--

14:39.628 --> 14:41.714
I apol… apologize.

14:41.797 --> 14:43.841
Please report, Satellite Center.

14:43.924 --> 14:47.052
Wind speeds are high
at the edge of the southern anticyclone,

14:47.136 --> 14:49.471
so we've put out a wind advisory
for the West Sea.

14:51.974 --> 14:53.058
Um, if you, uh…

14:53.142 --> 14:55.102
Thank… thank you very much.

15:02.735 --> 15:04.403
If you look at the satellite image,

15:04.486 --> 15:06.655
you can see that the clouds
are rotating clockwise

15:06.739 --> 15:08.699
with Gyeongbuk Province at the center.

15:08.782 --> 15:11.493
- Under such circumstances, the--
- Uh, no, no. Hold on.

15:11.577 --> 15:12.620
First, we need a briefing

15:12.703 --> 15:15.289
on the wind advisory situation
from two days ago.

15:15.789 --> 15:17.124
Sorry?

15:17.207 --> 15:20.252
It's chaos here
because of the high wind advisory.

15:24.131 --> 15:27.718
How can you keep the fishing ban?
This is our livelihood you're destroying.

15:27.801 --> 15:29.053
Last year's campaign,

15:29.136 --> 15:31.972
you said you'd make things better
for the fishermen, is this better, huh?

15:32.056 --> 15:34.099
You know crabs only have
a two-week season.

15:34.183 --> 15:36.977
And it's been two days since you've
banned us going there on our boats.

15:37.061 --> 15:38.270
We can't make a living, huh!

15:38.354 --> 15:41.023
Hey, come on! Do you know anybody
in the Coast Guard?

15:41.106 --> 15:43.859
Get the Governor or something
and do something about this situation.

15:43.943 --> 15:45.444
- Come on, man.
- Do it!

15:45.527 --> 15:46.362
Absolutely not.

15:46.445 --> 15:47.571
COAST GUARD
SENIOR SUPERINTENDENT YOO WON-CHEOL

15:47.655 --> 15:49.573
I am fully aware of the fishing situation.

15:49.657 --> 15:51.992
You can't sail
until the Meteorology Administration

15:52.076 --> 15:53.327
lowers its advisory.

15:54.161 --> 15:57.164
Uh, we only have
nine patrol boats available.

15:57.790 --> 15:59.959
And our team here
and the Coast Guard's team

16:00.042 --> 16:01.961
is only 32 people total.

16:02.044 --> 16:05.005
Now imagine if there's some sort
of accident off the coast.

16:05.089 --> 16:06.799
I can't risk that happening!

16:07.508 --> 16:10.344
I said I can't! And that's the end of it.

16:11.470 --> 16:12.638
GWANGJU REGIONAL OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

16:12.721 --> 16:15.933
This is happening right now.
Shouldn't you do something about it?

16:16.016 --> 16:17.768
Um, sea conditions in that area are…

16:24.566 --> 16:28.278
The current wave, uh, wave period
on the West Coast

16:28.362 --> 16:30.864
is down to 11.4 seconds.

16:30.948 --> 16:33.826
Uh, also, if you look
at other ocean readings…

16:34.451 --> 16:35.411
Uh, well, I…

16:35.995 --> 16:37.162
Let's help her out.

16:37.746 --> 16:39.248
Send the summary to her.

16:42.001 --> 16:43.293
Mm…

16:52.803 --> 16:54.179
I'm sorry.

16:56.015 --> 16:59.935
I'm so sorry. I haven't completely
analyzed the situation.

17:03.272 --> 17:06.275
Senior Forecaster Um,
could you please take over for me?

17:09.194 --> 17:12.614
The wave height is still unstable.

17:12.698 --> 17:16.076
Considering the fact that
there's also long wind drift distance,

17:16.744 --> 17:19.371
it doesn't appear very likely
that the wind will subside soon.

17:19.455 --> 17:20.789
No?

17:21.373 --> 17:24.710
Goodness gracious.

17:25.794 --> 17:29.048
Well, what does Mr. Lee think?

17:29.131 --> 17:31.717
The wave height is still high,
but the wave period has dropped

17:31.800 --> 17:34.053
from 14.5 to 11.4 seconds.

17:34.136 --> 17:35.345
The wind velocity is going down

17:35.429 --> 17:37.931
and there are fewer
large surface waves than before.

17:38.015 --> 17:40.392
So you don't agree with Mr. Um, then.

17:41.518 --> 17:42.478
I don't.

17:45.230 --> 17:46.690
What?

17:49.777 --> 17:53.614
It's the Administrator. It sounds like
it's about the wind advisory in Taean.

17:56.241 --> 17:58.452
I think local government's
pushing back on this one.

17:58.535 --> 18:00.954
- Oh, no.
- It's a little complicated.

18:01.038 --> 18:02.915
Director Jin, what are we going to do?

18:04.666 --> 18:08.629
Clearly, Mr. Um and Mr. Lee disagrees,
so as director, you should decide.

18:17.429 --> 18:19.640
Hey, Director.

18:19.723 --> 18:21.225
We'll observe the situation

18:21.308 --> 18:23.185
and consider
the wave height report carefully.

18:23.268 --> 18:26.814
TIME SECTION: A PERIOD OF 3 HOURS
IN WHICH WEATHER DATA IS UPDATED

18:32.528 --> 18:33.570
Yeah?

18:33.654 --> 18:35.948
All right.

18:36.031 --> 18:38.617
Okay. Well, we've decided
no changes for the time being.

18:38.700 --> 18:40.452
- Announce this.
- Right away.

18:41.453 --> 18:42.913
Meeting is now adjourned.

18:49.920 --> 18:51.046
I'm sorry, sir.

18:51.630 --> 18:53.799
About what? Being late, unprepared?

18:53.882 --> 18:56.051
Sorry, we need more time
to observe the data.

18:57.386 --> 18:59.513
If we need time, then we'll take it.
What's the matter?

19:00.514 --> 19:03.392
You're gonna get complaints
from all over the country.

19:04.476 --> 19:05.477
Look, Director.

19:06.061 --> 19:07.646
That's for me to handle.

19:07.729 --> 19:11.942
Your role should stay focused
on the weather and the team here.

19:13.110 --> 19:15.154
Right. I apologize.

19:16.196 --> 19:17.447
Knock it off.

19:18.740 --> 19:19.908
Great job, everyone.

19:19.992 --> 19:21.660
- Thank you very much, sir.
- Thank you, sir.

19:30.294 --> 19:33.630
I definitely told him that
you wanted to start the meeting.

19:34.214 --> 19:35.883
I told him two times.

19:40.804 --> 19:42.723
- Coffee run?
- Sure.

19:53.108 --> 19:54.193
Are you okay?

19:54.276 --> 19:58.280
Why? 'Cause I was late?
Unprepared? Or embarrassed myself?

19:58.363 --> 19:59.656
Because of your cold.

19:59.740 --> 20:01.408
You're sneezing a lot.

20:03.076 --> 20:06.246
I have rhinitis.
It acts up between seasons.

20:38.237 --> 20:39.696
I wanna buy this.

20:39.780 --> 20:44.159
NEIGHBORHOOD MARKET
SELLING AN AIR PURIFIER

20:44.243 --> 20:45.452
Thirty.

20:48.372 --> 20:49.456
Okay.

21:07.891 --> 21:09.726
What? Why are you still here?

21:14.898 --> 21:16.233
Haven't you heard?

21:16.316 --> 21:18.735
I've officially been assigned
to Headquarters.

21:19.278 --> 21:21.446
Why would they put you here?

21:21.530 --> 21:24.157
If you're so curious about it,
you can go ask HR.

21:24.241 --> 21:25.742
They handle all the personnel.

21:26.994 --> 21:29.204
And you're okay with seeing me
in the hall around here all the time?

21:29.288 --> 21:30.205
Uh-huh.

21:30.289 --> 21:33.417
It was my dream to work at Headquarters.
I'm gonna do my very best.

21:33.500 --> 21:37.379
I lost you
because I worked too hard for it. Right?

21:38.255 --> 21:41.341
You really think that I dumped you
for that reason?

21:41.925 --> 21:42.884
Then what's the reason?

21:42.968 --> 21:45.679
Did you really not put it together
or are you just playing coy?

21:52.519 --> 21:54.104
It's not important, though.

21:54.187 --> 21:57.190
You'll follow your road, and so will I.

22:01.028 --> 22:02.195
Chae!

22:02.696 --> 22:05.032
As you were, Reporter Chae.

22:12.122 --> 22:15.334
- Who's that?
- A Weather Alert Forecaster

22:15.417 --> 22:17.002
for Team Two, he just transferred here.

22:17.085 --> 22:19.004
So how do you know him?

22:19.087 --> 22:22.090
We barely know each other.
I met him a few times on the job.

22:22.174 --> 22:24.134
Oh, I see.

22:27.804 --> 22:30.140
COAST GUARD TELLS FISHERMEN
TO STAY ALERT FOR POSSIBLE ACCIDENTS

22:30.223 --> 22:31.725
STRONG WINDS EXPECTED ON THE WEST COAST

22:31.808 --> 22:32.851
REGULAR FERRY OPERATIONS SUSPENDED

22:32.934 --> 22:34.102
EXTRA CAUTION REQUIRED
FOR MARITIME ACCIDENTS

22:34.186 --> 22:36.897
Yes, the advisory
hasn't been lifted just yet.

22:36.980 --> 22:38.565
- Yes, that's right.
- Yes, I'm listening.

22:38.648 --> 22:41.818
Yes, we know that there
are difficulties with your operation.

22:41.902 --> 22:45.530
Still, there's enough wave activity
in the West Sea to warrant our concern.

22:45.614 --> 22:49.284
- Yes. The wave height is still…
- I know you're frustrated.

22:49.368 --> 22:50.702
We still have to be careful.

22:50.786 --> 22:52.496
We really wish
we could just lift the advisory.

22:52.579 --> 22:54.081
- Yeah.
- Yes, I like crab too.

22:54.164 --> 22:56.541
Believe me. We put these procedures in
for your safety.

22:56.625 --> 22:58.210
We create these guidelines…

22:58.293 --> 22:59.544
Yes, of course.

22:59.628 --> 23:02.589
- The… the forum?
- Okay.

23:03.173 --> 23:04.633
Yes, I understand.

23:04.716 --> 23:07.719
- Uh, yes. Just a minute. Thanks.
- Yes, okay.

23:07.803 --> 23:08.970
The forum's lost it.

23:12.474 --> 23:15.811
We're all suffering because the KMA
is making a big stink over nothing.

23:15.894 --> 23:18.980
It's not the weather that's gonna kill us.
It's the awful administration!

23:21.650 --> 23:24.611
Yeah, right!
There's no high winds around here.

23:24.694 --> 23:27.072
They don't know our ocean.

23:27.155 --> 23:29.408
I'll let you know
as soon as anything changes.

23:30.158 --> 23:31.910
- Yeah, yes.
- Oh, yes, of course.

23:31.993 --> 23:33.537
For safety, okay?

23:39.376 --> 23:40.794
We can't go on like this.

23:41.545 --> 23:42.963
- Director Han.
- Yes?

23:43.046 --> 23:44.923
You have to go to the Chief Team

23:45.006 --> 23:47.134
and at least have them approve
a preliminary advisory.

23:47.717 --> 23:49.094
"Advisory"?

23:49.177 --> 23:51.513
Yeah, we have to put out some info
about these waves out there

23:51.596 --> 23:53.348
when we might lift the advisory.

23:53.432 --> 23:56.017
Otherwise, all we're gonna do today
is answer calls.

23:56.101 --> 23:57.519
I'll ask them, then.

23:58.103 --> 24:00.480
Assistant Director,
which team is in charge right now?

24:01.690 --> 24:02.858
Team Two right now, I believe.

24:06.361 --> 24:07.737
Oh, man.

24:08.405 --> 24:10.991
Aren't you uncomfortable
seeing me every single day like this?

24:11.074 --> 24:12.576
Oh, is it hard for you to see me?

24:12.659 --> 24:14.453
It sounds like you're the one
who should go.

24:14.536 --> 24:17.080
I think you'd do great in Geneva,
you asshole.

24:17.164 --> 24:19.791
Asshole!

24:24.087 --> 24:25.088
What is it?

24:26.047 --> 24:29.134
The high wind advisory issued
on the Central West Sea,

24:29.217 --> 24:32.053
- it's lasted 40 hours.
- And so?

24:32.137 --> 24:35.682
It would improve things if you provided us
with an estimated end time--

24:35.765 --> 24:38.018
Ah, you must not have heard
the meeting decision.

24:38.101 --> 24:39.853
Because of the dangerous state
of the surface waves,

24:39.936 --> 24:42.522
we can't go any lower
than our current state of wind advisory

24:42.606 --> 24:43.815
until we have more information.

24:43.899 --> 24:46.610
That's why we'd like to give
a preliminary update.

24:47.194 --> 24:50.071
About when the waves might calm down,
this afternoon, tomorrow morning?

24:50.155 --> 24:52.282
The wave height value
is still unstable.

24:52.365 --> 24:55.660
I can't send out an expected advisory
end time just to go and revise it.

24:55.744 --> 24:57.787
Let's leave things as they are.

25:02.334 --> 25:03.627
You can, though.

25:08.215 --> 25:09.424
What do you mean?

25:10.425 --> 25:11.426
You could send it.

25:11.510 --> 25:13.845
You're drawing things out
on purpose out of spite.

25:13.929 --> 25:15.931
You're trying to hurt me now, aren't you?

25:17.807 --> 25:21.520
Are you saying that I'm ruining
the crab fishermen's livelihood

25:21.603 --> 25:24.272
just to make things a little
inconvenient for you here?

25:24.356 --> 25:26.483
- Aren't you?
- Listen, Mr. Han Ki-jun!

25:26.566 --> 25:27.984
I can help with this.

25:31.112 --> 25:33.865
I handle Severe Weather Alerts,
so I can talk about it with you.

25:35.784 --> 25:38.036
Do you know what it's like
over in our office right now?

25:38.119 --> 25:40.288
We can't work while we have
dozens of calls coming in all the time

25:40.372 --> 25:42.415
from local governments
mad about the boats.

25:42.499 --> 25:44.251
How can we take care
of any other business?

25:44.834 --> 25:48.129
Shouldn't the Spokesperson's Office
at least be able to do its job?

25:48.213 --> 25:49.297
What?

25:49.965 --> 25:50.924
"Its job"?

25:51.007 --> 25:53.051
Everyone on the Chief Team
is busy with the data.

25:53.635 --> 25:55.762
All we're talking about
is this wind advisory.

25:55.845 --> 25:56.972
We didn't even have lunch.

25:57.055 --> 26:00.350
Everyone here is working their ass off
to make sure the reports are accurate.

26:00.433 --> 26:03.228
Handling complaint calls
is one of your most basic duties.

26:03.311 --> 26:04.771
Our entire staff's on a crunch,

26:04.854 --> 26:06.982
and you came over here
to complain you job is hard?

26:07.065 --> 26:09.025
That's why you came all the way over here?

26:10.735 --> 26:13.697
This isn't your place
or your concern, so back off.

26:14.698 --> 26:16.241
Well, I do the alerts, so--

26:16.324 --> 26:19.786
So what, huh? Just wait,
and I'll talk to your director.

26:20.537 --> 26:22.247
That's enough, Mr. Lee.

26:24.040 --> 26:25.959
Mr. Han, you should go back
to your office.

26:26.543 --> 26:27.377
Hmm?

26:28.503 --> 26:29.796
Um…

26:30.964 --> 26:33.091
Hey, I… I should go or…

26:33.174 --> 26:34.801
When there's severe weather,

26:35.927 --> 26:38.972
lack of caution leads to death,
are you aware of that?

26:39.055 --> 26:42.851
It's not a situation anyone would
draw out for some sad revenge.

26:43.518 --> 26:46.521
So go back and wait for our forecast.

26:55.488 --> 26:58.783
- Well, that's still--
- Go! And stay out of here.

27:29.522 --> 27:30.398
Is she okay?

27:31.399 --> 27:32.275
Hmm?

27:33.026 --> 27:34.527
Ha-kyung, well, she, uh…

27:35.111 --> 27:37.864
She acts like she has
a few screws loose in her head.

27:38.531 --> 27:39.699
I get it, though.

27:39.783 --> 27:42.077
Going to work every day must be hell.

27:43.328 --> 27:46.498
It's rough enough that she has to see
that bastard Han Ki-jun's face

27:46.581 --> 27:50.710
all over there all the time,
but her co-workers know all about it.

27:50.794 --> 27:53.880
So all she can do is ignore him
and keep working.

27:53.963 --> 27:55.507
Would you be okay if you were her?

27:58.343 --> 27:59.969
What, Mom? What's going on?

28:04.099 --> 28:05.433
Oh, Ha-kyung.

28:05.517 --> 28:07.644
Uh, if you're having trouble at work--

28:07.727 --> 28:08.895
I'm busy right now, Ma.

28:08.978 --> 28:10.563
Oh, okay.

28:14.234 --> 28:15.235
I told you, Ma.

28:15.318 --> 28:18.321
The best thing for us to do
is leave her alone.

28:18.405 --> 28:22.200
She sounded kind of unwell.
Oh, Ha-kyung's sick.

28:38.133 --> 28:38.967
Here.

28:39.592 --> 28:40.802
I told you it's rhinitis.

28:42.095 --> 28:43.471
You're not as sharp as you look.

28:49.394 --> 28:50.687
You have a fever.

28:56.025 --> 28:57.152
Take one right now.

29:02.699 --> 29:03.908
What do you think you're doing?

29:03.992 --> 29:05.660
It's just part of the job.

29:05.744 --> 29:06.953
Sucking up to the director.

29:16.755 --> 29:20.300
Don't worry, though. I won't ask you out
just because we hooked up.

29:23.344 --> 29:24.596
Take it now, okay?

29:42.530 --> 29:43.698
Oh, jeez.

29:44.699 --> 29:46.534
Hey!

29:46.618 --> 29:49.287
Oh, wait a second, eh?

29:49.871 --> 29:51.664
Yeah. Hey?

29:53.249 --> 29:55.001
The ocean's peaceful right now.

29:56.294 --> 29:58.797
I could swim in it,
so we could definitely sail.

29:59.881 --> 30:00.965
Huh?

30:01.466 --> 30:03.510
Our sailors have gone to sea
more times in their life

30:03.593 --> 30:04.636
than they've gone to the bathroom.

30:04.719 --> 30:06.179
Uh, how far out?

30:06.888 --> 30:09.307
Yeah. How does it look to you right now?

30:10.433 --> 30:11.392
Oh, okay.

30:12.101 --> 30:13.645
Oh, and can you describe, uh,

30:13.728 --> 30:16.147
the shape of the clouds
and the wind pattern in detail?

30:17.106 --> 30:18.399
Yes. Uh-huh.

30:22.695 --> 30:24.322
I checked on the situation on the ground.

30:24.405 --> 30:27.116
There are surface waves along the coast,
but it gets calm far out.

30:27.200 --> 30:28.409
Who told you that?

30:28.493 --> 30:30.954
Captain I met
when I was on a weather ship.

30:31.037 --> 30:32.539
He knows the weather around
the coast of Taean

30:32.622 --> 30:33.748
as well as he knows his palm.

30:34.332 --> 30:37.168
Each year, around 18 boats
are capsized due to surface waves

30:37.252 --> 30:39.587
and in those accidents,
32 sailors have died,

30:39.671 --> 30:43.466
and they all would have said they know
the sea as well as they know their palms.

30:43.550 --> 30:45.426
The wind on the sea surface is weak.

30:45.510 --> 30:48.304
It is risky
with the elevated wave height out there.

30:48.888 --> 30:51.516
Still, Mr. Lee's correct.
The wind velocity is declining.

30:52.684 --> 30:53.726
- It's true.
- If we at least

30:53.810 --> 30:57.188
lower the advisory to a warning,
the bigger ships could sail.

30:57.272 --> 31:00.900
Then, there would be less pressure on you
and on the fishermen too.

31:01.484 --> 31:02.735
If we let the big ones go,

31:02.819 --> 31:04.737
the small ones are going
to follow one by one.

31:04.821 --> 31:05.989
Do you think we can control it?

31:06.072 --> 31:08.825
No one can.
That's why the Coast Guard's worried.

31:09.409 --> 31:11.160
So you wanna maintain the advisory order?

31:16.165 --> 31:17.750
What do you think?

31:19.586 --> 31:21.629
If you're on the fence with it,

31:22.630 --> 31:24.048
just follow the numbers.

31:26.676 --> 31:30.430
But it's crab season, and we can't ignore
the local fishermen's situation.

31:31.264 --> 31:34.517
Or you go
with Forecaster Lee's gut feeling,

31:34.601 --> 31:36.769
and then reduce the alert.

31:37.854 --> 31:42.025
Who knows? Maybe the Dragon King
of the Sea will calm the waves.

31:45.320 --> 31:47.196
You talk like you're not involved here.

31:49.574 --> 31:52.410
Well, in the end, I'm not the one
who has to make the decision.

31:52.493 --> 31:53.703
It's on your head.

31:54.329 --> 31:55.747
Ah.

31:55.830 --> 31:56.873
Okay.

32:21.856 --> 32:23.441
Spokesperson's Office, this is Ki-jun.

32:23.524 --> 32:24.734
This is the decision made

32:24.817 --> 32:27.445
by the Chief Forecaster's Team
at 3:23 p.m.

32:27.528 --> 32:28.529
Sir, sir.

32:28.613 --> 32:30.823
- It's the Chief Team.
- Are they lifting it?

32:30.907 --> 32:31.824
Okay.

32:32.533 --> 32:33.618
Yes, go ahead.

32:33.701 --> 32:36.829
The wind and wave height on the West Coast
is down to a warning level,

32:36.913 --> 32:38.748
but the deviation
of the significant wave height

32:38.831 --> 32:40.124
in that area is large,

32:40.208 --> 32:42.502
so until nine o'clock,
monitoring will continue,

32:42.585 --> 32:45.505
then we'll decide whether
to lift it or drop it to a warning.

32:45.588 --> 32:47.674
Uh, Director Jin. What are you saying?

32:49.592 --> 32:52.136
Chief Director. Direc… Director Jin!

32:56.975 --> 32:57.850
Hmm?

33:01.562 --> 33:04.065
- Phones will be on fire again.
- Yes, hello. Spokesperson's Office.

33:04.148 --> 33:06.275
Yes, yes.

33:06.359 --> 33:08.486
Yes, hello.
This is the Media Interface Office.

33:08.569 --> 33:11.990
Yes, it's been extended
just a little bit. I'm sorry.

33:12.073 --> 33:14.075
Okay, I'll send out the update
and memo right now.

33:14.158 --> 33:15.034
Okay.

33:17.954 --> 33:19.789
I didn't expect your team
to be so conservative.

33:20.873 --> 33:23.918
I made the decision
based on data, so what's wrong?

33:24.002 --> 33:25.211
There's one more thing
you have to consider

33:25.294 --> 33:26.796
aside from the charts and reports.

33:27.588 --> 33:28.715
Intuition.

33:28.798 --> 33:31.509
Okay? And I know
I almost always get it right.

33:33.553 --> 33:35.221
- Forecaster.
- Yes?

33:37.140 --> 33:39.851
Our job is a science.
If you want to stay on my team,

33:39.934 --> 33:42.520
please base your theories only
on science from now on,

33:42.603 --> 33:43.688
not your intuition.

33:43.771 --> 33:45.023
Got it?

33:51.362 --> 33:53.698
From right now, two o'clock
to nine o'clock tonight,

33:53.781 --> 33:56.117
the high wind advisory
on the West coast will be sustained.

33:56.200 --> 33:58.286
I'll send that now.

34:02.081 --> 34:03.624
HIGH WIND WARNING EXTENSION

34:03.708 --> 34:04.917
SEND NOTICE?
YES

34:05.001 --> 34:05.960
THE NOTICE HAS BEEN SENT

34:06.044 --> 34:08.212
WEST SEA COAST GUARD STATION

34:12.967 --> 34:16.429
NOTICE
HIGH WIND WARNING EXTENSION

34:18.473 --> 34:20.183
APPLICABLE AREA
CENTRAL WEST SEA, EAST SEA

34:27.690 --> 34:28.858
Seriously?

34:29.692 --> 34:32.070
Oh, really?

34:32.987 --> 34:33.905
Yeah?

34:34.655 --> 34:36.074
Yeah.

34:36.908 --> 34:39.327
This weather alert's gonna kill us all.

34:39.410 --> 34:41.162
It's gonna bankrupt us all.

34:41.245 --> 34:43.289
All right, that's it.

34:43.372 --> 34:45.917
No ships are setting sail today.

34:46.000 --> 34:47.418
- Again?
- Are you kidding?

34:47.502 --> 34:49.796
- The weather is getting even.
- Come on.

34:49.879 --> 34:51.881
- This is shit.
- I can't believe it.

35:02.183 --> 35:04.060
Who will cook all this food?

35:05.019 --> 35:07.814
I won't make you do it,
so stop complaining.

35:07.897 --> 35:10.024
Go over to the seafood counter

35:10.108 --> 35:12.401
and ask them
when the loach is coming in, okay?

35:12.485 --> 35:14.195
You're making fish soup tonight?

35:14.278 --> 35:16.155
Ha-kyung can't even eat fish soup

35:16.239 --> 35:18.866
- cause her stomach's no good.
- And so?

35:18.950 --> 35:20.993
Oh, yeah.

35:22.870 --> 35:25.248
And fish soup at home takes way too long.

35:25.331 --> 35:27.917
You can order it online
and it will become fresh the next day.

35:28.000 --> 35:29.293
It's not right.

35:33.506 --> 35:35.633
GREEN ONIONS
2,790 WON

35:37.468 --> 35:39.303
Oh, my gosh, is that really you?

35:39.971 --> 35:41.556
Soo-ja, hi.

35:41.639 --> 35:42.557
Mrs. Lee!

35:43.141 --> 35:45.017
Gosh, long time no see.

35:45.685 --> 35:48.104
Have you… Are you feeling all right?

35:48.187 --> 35:50.565
You haven't come to your exercise class.

35:51.649 --> 35:54.068
Well, my youngest daughter
just had a child.

35:54.152 --> 35:55.862
I was in the US for a few months,

35:55.945 --> 35:58.030
just to give them a hand.

35:58.114 --> 36:00.658
Ah. Is it a girl or a…

36:01.242 --> 36:03.286
- A girl!
- Wow, that's great.

36:03.369 --> 36:05.663
Daughters are just so wonderful.

36:05.746 --> 36:07.623
Your younger daughter
just got married, yeah?

36:08.457 --> 36:12.003
I got the invitation,
and I felt so bad I couldn't be there.

36:12.086 --> 36:13.045
Oh, wait a second.

36:13.129 --> 36:15.590
I can give you a gift for her.
Hold on a moment.

36:15.673 --> 36:17.800
Oh, no. No, no, no. It's all right.

36:18.634 --> 36:20.052
Now, come on.

36:20.136 --> 36:22.054
You gave so much
when my youngest had her wedding.

36:22.138 --> 36:24.640
No, no, I said, uh, no, no.

36:24.724 --> 36:26.809
Uh…

36:28.186 --> 36:30.396
She's not married.

36:30.479 --> 36:31.397
Huh?

36:31.981 --> 36:35.276
- Well, they called off the wedding.
- Oh, why?

36:35.359 --> 36:37.653
You were bragging
about how he's some hotshot

36:37.737 --> 36:40.615
at the same office as her, and I…

36:40.698 --> 36:43.534
You bragged about that jerk, Han Ki-jun?

36:43.618 --> 36:47.538
- Shut it.
- What happened? Did something go wrong?

36:47.622 --> 36:49.457
Uh, no, it's all right.

36:49.540 --> 36:52.710
It all happens, you know.
Divorces, too, or…

36:53.294 --> 36:57.798
I made them call it off
because he was wrong for her.

36:57.882 --> 36:59.425
Oh…

36:59.508 --> 37:02.220
I can't imagine how you must be feeling.

37:03.012 --> 37:04.805
Your older daughter got divorced

37:04.889 --> 37:07.808
and your youngest
lost her fiancé too, hmm?

37:08.434 --> 37:10.228
Did you hear? I told her to cancel it.

37:10.311 --> 37:13.564
I'm glad to see you're doing okay
after all you've been through, huh?

37:14.315 --> 37:16.150
I would have been so devastated.

37:16.234 --> 37:18.611
Aren't there worse things that can happen?

37:18.694 --> 37:22.698
And also, listen more carefully
when I'm talking to you, huh?

37:22.782 --> 37:26.452
My daughters, my girls,
they didn't get left, okay? They left.

37:26.535 --> 37:27.954
You, you tell her.

37:28.037 --> 37:31.624
- You divorced him, huh? Huh?
- Let's go, Ma.

37:31.707 --> 37:32.792
- Wait a second, okay?
- Later.

37:32.875 --> 37:35.920
- Why are you over here twisting my words?
- Mom, let's go.

37:36.712 --> 37:38.047
They have really good loach, okay?

37:38.130 --> 37:39.257
- They have it?
- They have it.

37:39.340 --> 37:41.342
- Let's go get it.
- Let's go. Let's just go.

37:50.643 --> 37:51.602
Goodbye.

37:52.270 --> 37:54.438
They opened a new Kalguksu
place near the office.

37:54.522 --> 37:56.107
Oh, sounds good. Sounds good.

37:56.774 --> 37:58.317
Uh, are you… are you, uh…

37:58.401 --> 38:00.194
Hmm, go on and enjoy yourselves.

38:00.278 --> 38:01.654
See you tomorrow, then.

38:02.154 --> 38:03.072
- All right.
- Let's go.

38:03.155 --> 38:04.907
- Is the place good?
- I heard it's great.

38:06.867 --> 38:08.160
Aren't you leaving?

38:08.244 --> 38:11.747
Oh, yeah. Oh, so stiff.

38:15.960 --> 38:17.003
Uh…

38:17.545 --> 38:19.880
- See you tomorrow, then.
- All right. See you tomorrow.

38:24.135 --> 38:25.928
- Mr. Um.
- Huh?

38:27.179 --> 38:29.015
Don't you have something
to say to me right now?

38:29.098 --> 38:30.308
Um, not really.

38:33.728 --> 38:35.896
Why? Do you have something to say?

38:39.942 --> 38:44.405
It's okay if you don't like me,
but work is work, and…

38:45.156 --> 38:46.157
Of course.

38:46.782 --> 38:49.243
It's my fault I was late to our meeting.

38:49.327 --> 38:53.164
However, you still could have covered
for me at the start of it.

38:53.247 --> 38:54.415
Oh.

38:55.374 --> 38:57.376
Then you should have ordered me
to do that.

39:00.046 --> 39:02.965
Well, I know it can be uncomfortable

39:03.049 --> 39:06.052
to have someone who is so much
more experience as your subordinate.

39:06.135 --> 39:07.636
I'm sure there's pressure.

39:07.720 --> 39:11.098
But when it comes to work,
you're my superior, and so,

39:11.182 --> 39:13.434
I'm gonna do what you say
that I should do.

39:15.269 --> 39:17.480
So don't be afraid to give me orders
when you need to.

39:19.815 --> 39:21.859
I know what it's like to be there.

39:21.942 --> 39:25.571
If you're not quick enough
on the draw, you get complaints.

39:26.364 --> 39:27.740
And if your call's controversial,

39:27.823 --> 39:30.284
you're always gonna have people
speaking out against you.

39:30.368 --> 39:33.621
And if you don't make the hard calls,
well, everyone ignores you.

39:35.498 --> 39:36.874
You know what I'm saying?

39:37.458 --> 39:38.793
Yeah, I get it.

39:40.169 --> 39:42.588
Even so, you'll still need time
to adjust here.

39:43.297 --> 39:44.382
I promise…

39:45.007 --> 39:46.467
to not be so late.

39:47.426 --> 39:49.678
However, if something
like that does happen again

39:49.762 --> 39:52.139
due to an unforeseen cause,

39:52.890 --> 39:55.810
come in where I would
and get everything going.

39:58.437 --> 39:59.772
That's a command.

40:02.650 --> 40:04.652
Yeah. See you tomorrow, then.

40:05.694 --> 40:06.821
See you tomorrow.

40:30.428 --> 40:31.387
Yeah?

40:31.470 --> 40:33.848
Ha-kyung,
you should come home late tonight.

40:34.890 --> 40:35.724
Why?

40:35.808 --> 40:39.228
Mrs. Bae started downing soju
and she's not stopping.

40:54.910 --> 40:59.665
 Okay. I got it.

41:14.597 --> 41:17.475
Hey, could I get 20,000 off
on the air purifier

41:17.558 --> 41:19.435
if I come pick it up myself?

41:20.394 --> 41:22.771
Can you come
to this address tonight and take it?

41:23.439 --> 41:24.315
Yeah.

41:25.983 --> 41:29.278
APARTMENT 1201, BUILDING 308,
7, SHINJEONG-RO, DONGJAK-GU

41:50.049 --> 41:51.509
- Whoa!
- What the…

41:51.592 --> 41:54.053
Gross.

41:57.932 --> 41:59.225
PLEASE KNOCK

42:04.813 --> 42:07.107
You know you don't live here
all by yourself, right?

42:07.191 --> 42:10.528
- Mm-hmm.
- Why didn't you lock the bathroom door?

42:11.278 --> 42:13.405
I'm not used to it yet.

42:13.489 --> 42:15.032
Oh, my god.

42:26.544 --> 42:28.546
- Isn't this your home?
- Huh?

42:29.088 --> 42:30.631
Why are you just standing there?

42:46.272 --> 42:48.399
- Here, have some fruit.
- Thanks.

42:53.279 --> 42:55.656
That had to have given you a startle.

42:56.532 --> 42:58.867
Your dad is so silly, right?

43:00.119 --> 43:00.953
Where is he now?

43:03.789 --> 43:06.041
Please, you shouldn't be too hard
on your father.

43:07.084 --> 43:10.754
He just doesn't know some things yet.
He spent a lot of time away.

43:10.838 --> 43:12.214
If you could be kinder--

43:12.298 --> 43:14.717
- Neither do I.
- Huh?

43:16.302 --> 43:18.762
I don't know some things either.

43:21.390 --> 43:23.434
I've never lived with Dad before.

44:10.022 --> 44:12.691
Seriously?

44:30.292 --> 44:33.337
I'M OFF TO WORK.
I MADE BREAKFAST SO MAKE SURE TO EAT!

44:46.350 --> 44:47.768
Have you heard?

44:47.851 --> 44:51.188
That lady who is supposed
to marry Deputy Director Han?

44:51.271 --> 44:52.439
Hmm?

44:52.523 --> 44:55.025
She made a whole scene
in the office yesterday.

44:55.109 --> 44:57.986
She slapped Deputy Director Han
in front of all those people.

44:59.947 --> 45:01.198
Um…

45:01.281 --> 45:04.702
And promised she'd never give up
their apartment.

45:34.356 --> 45:35.691
You're home early.

45:35.774 --> 45:37.192
Sorry, I didn't clean up.

45:37.860 --> 45:39.903
I ran out of time before work.

45:41.572 --> 45:43.866
It must've been hard
putting everything away.

45:43.949 --> 45:45.159
Yu-jin.

45:47.161 --> 45:50.873
I told you at least put your plates away
after you're done with them.

45:50.956 --> 45:52.624
I was busy, though. You understand.

45:52.708 --> 45:54.626
I told you, they breed fruit flies.

45:55.335 --> 45:59.256
Those were from the banana peel
that you threw away in the regular trash.

45:59.339 --> 46:01.133
- That was only once.
- It was not, though.

46:01.216 --> 46:02.176
I…

46:03.427 --> 46:06.263
Forget it. Okay?

46:06.346 --> 46:10.184
Okay. You cleaned up,
so I'll go take out the trash.

46:19.485 --> 46:23.572
- Oh, no.
- Why can't you do anything right?

46:25.699 --> 46:28.035
What about you?
What have you done that's great?

46:28.118 --> 46:30.412
Me? Wha… What have I done wrong?

46:33.957 --> 46:36.502
The apartment you had with that woman,
did you take care of it?

46:37.211 --> 46:38.796
No. No, you didn't, huh?

46:40.339 --> 46:41.632
How did you know that?

46:41.715 --> 46:43.717
Everyone at work
knows about her. Everyone.

46:44.384 --> 46:47.346
You know the rent's so high here
'cause it's a short-term lease, right?

46:47.429 --> 46:49.973
We were supposed to move out
as soon as you got your money, okay?

46:50.057 --> 46:53.602
When's that happening?
We have no idea what we're doing.

46:54.645 --> 46:55.938
You don't have to worry about it.

46:56.021 --> 46:59.233
Why? Didn't she say
she's holding on to it?

46:59.316 --> 47:02.277
The nerve of that woman, I swear to you.

47:02.361 --> 47:05.572
You said half the apartment's yours.
Why can't you fight her or something?

47:08.325 --> 47:11.203
It cost us 20 million won,
and you deposited 5.

47:11.286 --> 47:12.830
I paid the rest on my own.

47:12.913 --> 47:16.583
And I also covered the deposit,
down payment, and the mortgage on my own.

47:17.292 --> 47:19.711
Uh, then what does that mean?

47:19.795 --> 47:22.506
Halvsies? You must be joking.

47:22.589 --> 47:24.550
That's low, even for you.

47:26.552 --> 47:30.931
Anyway, it's not good for either of us
if things get complicated at work.

47:31.473 --> 47:33.350
This is how it is.
That's all you have to know.

47:49.783 --> 47:50.701
Yu-jin.

47:53.036 --> 47:54.955
I told you not to do this kind of stuff.

47:55.038 --> 47:57.708
- I can just take it out on my way out.
- Just leave it.

47:58.333 --> 48:00.002
I don't want you getting your hands dirty.

48:00.085 --> 48:02.379
Pss. All right.

48:38.707 --> 48:40.584
I really used to love sitting here.

48:55.390 --> 48:57.267
Lee Si-woo, why are you here?

49:01.063 --> 49:03.398
Huh? This is the right place.

49:05.025 --> 49:07.361
NEIGHBORHOOD MARKET

49:07.444 --> 49:08.987
Are you "issue"?

49:09.613 --> 49:11.198
Wait, and you're "jjin"?

49:31.259 --> 49:32.678
Don't look around.

49:34.304 --> 49:35.514
Oh, okay.

49:40.102 --> 49:41.103
This is it?

49:41.728 --> 49:42.854
Just go.

49:43.480 --> 49:45.607
You know why
I don't want to sell it to you.

49:47.401 --> 49:48.360
Yeah.

49:52.280 --> 49:54.741
- You're throwing this out?
- Come on, just go.

49:58.662 --> 49:59.663
Okay.

50:07.087 --> 50:08.922
- Oh, Director.
- What now?

50:09.464 --> 50:12.092
Is this your first time
selling something online?

50:12.175 --> 50:13.051
Yeah.

50:13.135 --> 50:15.303
I mean, this air purifier.

50:15.387 --> 50:17.639
You said you've only
tried it once to test it.

50:17.723 --> 50:19.516
Then it's almost brand new,

50:19.599 --> 50:21.476
and it's the number one model
of this kind.

50:21.560 --> 50:23.603
You could easily get 400,000 won for it.

50:23.687 --> 50:26.023
Why would you ever wanna settle
for 300,000?

50:27.607 --> 50:29.443
And this speaker is a limited edition,

50:29.526 --> 50:31.737
so you can't find it anywhere,
not even overseas.

50:31.820 --> 50:33.280
- Really?
- Yes.

50:33.363 --> 50:36.450
If you sell it to an audiophile, you can
get more than the original asking price.

50:36.533 --> 50:39.870
But you're selling a top-end FB speaker
like this one for half-price.

50:39.953 --> 50:41.496
This is not a sale. It's a giveaway.

50:42.497 --> 50:43.331
What's FB?

50:43.415 --> 50:46.418
Full box. It's the item
in its original package.

50:46.501 --> 50:47.377
Oh.

50:48.211 --> 50:52.507
Oh! And also, these pictures
of the products you posted on here.

50:53.842 --> 50:56.011
There are lots of scams
on this sort of site.

50:57.054 --> 51:00.265
So you should write your username
and the date on a piece of paper like this

51:00.348 --> 51:01.391
and take a picture with it.

51:01.475 --> 51:02.726
So they know you're for real.

51:03.310 --> 51:04.644
- Hmm.
- Like this.

51:04.728 --> 51:05.562
YOSE AUTHENTIC SPEAKER
MAY 10TH JJIN

51:05.645 --> 51:06.813
Like this right here.

51:06.897 --> 51:08.982
Yeah, post the picture here.

51:09.066 --> 51:11.068
- Now you upload? Okay.
- Username. Yes.

51:11.151 --> 51:13.153
Date here. "No haggling."

51:13.236 --> 51:15.781
- So this means it's already a bargain.
- Uh-huh. Mm-hmm.

51:16.323 --> 51:17.532
- FB.
- Mm-hmm.

51:18.200 --> 51:20.077
Overseas limited edition.

51:20.160 --> 51:22.370
- And shippable.
- "Ship…"

51:32.589 --> 51:33.715
Don't worry, though.

51:33.799 --> 51:35.634
I won't ask you out
just because we hooked up.

51:36.760 --> 51:37.844
Why?

51:39.554 --> 51:41.389
- Huh?
- Oh?

51:42.849 --> 51:44.935
What? Why?

51:45.560 --> 51:47.687
You were the one
that just asked me why, though.

51:47.771 --> 51:50.065
No, I… I didn't. I wouldn't just…

51:53.151 --> 51:55.612
- Did I, um, do something wrong?
- No.

51:56.279 --> 51:57.781
Why would you have?

51:58.907 --> 52:00.700
Why are you acting so nervous right now?

52:02.035 --> 52:03.411
I'm not nervous at all.

52:09.167 --> 52:10.502
What?

52:15.924 --> 52:16.925
Oh, hey!

52:18.510 --> 52:19.886
- A buyer?
- Yeah!

52:19.970 --> 52:22.055
- Oh…
- Buying it right now.

52:22.722 --> 52:23.849
Oh, that's great.

52:27.644 --> 52:29.020
Thanks so much for this.

52:30.188 --> 52:31.273
Thank you.

52:46.454 --> 52:47.831
You were so helpful.

52:48.498 --> 52:50.333
Well, then you can buy me dinner.

52:52.085 --> 52:54.504
- What are you saying?
- I'm just hungry.

52:55.088 --> 52:56.256
Does it have to be more?

52:57.883 --> 52:58.925
No, of course.

52:59.509 --> 53:01.136
What would you like, Forecaster?

53:01.887 --> 53:03.930
I'm fine with anything.

53:05.015 --> 53:06.057
Let's go.

54:36.231 --> 54:38.525
It's hard
when the season's changing.

54:38.608 --> 54:42.529
You can't really say
if it'll be cold or hot.

54:42.612 --> 54:46.783
But just like the summer heat
that comes after spring goes by,

54:47.492 --> 54:50.370
after this vague
and difficult period is over,

54:50.453 --> 54:54.207
flowers of a new season
will bloom before you know it.

54:56.501 --> 54:58.336
Here's that special
that you ordered.

55:07.929 --> 55:09.848
You're selling your place too?

55:10.557 --> 55:11.599
Mm-hmm.

55:11.683 --> 55:14.144
- That's a shame.
- It is.

55:14.227 --> 55:15.812
I would just live there, if I were you.

55:16.438 --> 55:18.231
You wouldn't understand it, but--

55:18.315 --> 55:19.607
I think I do understand.

55:20.358 --> 55:22.527
Ah, yeah.

55:23.778 --> 55:26.656
Anyway, that place
has too many weird memories.

55:26.740 --> 55:28.325
I really just have to leave there.

55:28.408 --> 55:30.660
You can't just toss everything he touched.

55:30.744 --> 55:32.120
What about your heart?

55:32.203 --> 55:34.539
You wouldn't wanna
just throw that away, would you?

55:34.622 --> 55:36.416
Just because somebody's been in there?

55:37.542 --> 55:39.210
Well, it will help me to let go of him.

55:40.670 --> 55:42.505
You'll have some regrets
either way, you know.

55:44.466 --> 55:46.676
It's not like you can just
turn back the clock.

55:46.760 --> 55:49.346
You don't mean anything
to that person any longer.

55:50.305 --> 55:53.641
So it feels unfair that you're the one
who has to suffer the loss.

55:59.189 --> 56:00.815
I was hoping you wouldn't go through that.

56:05.737 --> 56:06.905
You're concerned?

56:07.655 --> 56:10.367
Well, as someone
who went through it, don't.

56:10.950 --> 56:12.285
I'll be all right.

56:16.706 --> 56:17.832
Hey, your medicine.

56:18.500 --> 56:19.709
Eat your food.

56:32.430 --> 56:33.556
What are you doing?

56:34.599 --> 56:37.060
Hmm, you took it.

56:39.938 --> 56:41.272
Your fever broke.

56:48.321 --> 56:52.200
Like I said, it's hard
when the season is changing.

56:55.578 --> 56:57.580
- Oh, how cool.
- Welcome.

56:58.581 --> 56:59.624
- How many people?
- Three.

56:59.707 --> 57:01.376
- Three? Just a second.
- What is it?

57:02.669 --> 57:04.087
Over there.

57:04.170 --> 57:06.172
I think that table's available.

57:06.256 --> 57:08.633
We'll show you to your table
after we finish cleaning it off.

57:08.716 --> 57:09.843
- But why are you hiding?
- Shh!

57:11.594 --> 57:12.846
What do we do?

57:13.430 --> 57:14.514
They can't see us.

57:14.597 --> 57:15.557
Doing what?

57:16.808 --> 57:19.227
Don't you get it?
This thing between you and me?

57:21.521 --> 57:23.231
They're gonna see us.

57:25.567 --> 57:27.068
Hey, where are you going?

57:29.028 --> 57:30.447
This can't be.

57:31.072 --> 57:32.699
- Just a moment.
- All right.

57:34.075 --> 57:35.577
- Oh?
- Oh!

57:36.077 --> 57:37.579
Hey, what are you guys doing here?

57:37.662 --> 57:39.622
Director Shin said the chicken here
is really good.

57:39.706 --> 57:40.999
What are you doing?

57:41.082 --> 57:44.210
Oh, someone I know said
the chicken was good,

57:44.294 --> 57:45.795
so, so we had a drink together.

57:47.547 --> 57:48.882
Oh, she's a friend?

57:50.925 --> 57:51.843
Oh!

58:02.395 --> 58:03.938
Uh, never mind.

58:04.022 --> 58:05.607
I thought I saw someone I knew.

58:13.072 --> 58:14.866
Well…

58:16.784 --> 58:19.162
Well, if your friend's
already gone, do you wanna join us?

58:19.245 --> 58:21.664
Uh, no, something came up, so…

58:22.248 --> 58:23.875
- Have a great time.
- Ah.

58:23.958 --> 58:25.335
- See you.
- Goodbye.

58:25.418 --> 58:26.836
All right.

58:28.755 --> 58:30.840
- Follow me, please.
- Ah, thanks.

58:50.276 --> 58:51.110
Come here.

59:01.579 --> 59:02.622
How'd it go?

59:02.705 --> 59:04.791
No one suspected us, did they?

59:06.417 --> 59:07.752
Or did they?

59:07.835 --> 59:09.337
What's going on?

59:10.213 --> 59:11.422
What do you mean?

59:11.506 --> 59:12.590
With us.

59:13.091 --> 59:14.842
Do we have something
to hide from the others?

59:16.261 --> 59:18.930
Uh, I'm just worried that us
being seen here

59:19.013 --> 59:21.140
would stir up a misunderstanding.

59:21.224 --> 59:25.853
Rumors about us or they would think
we're maybe dating or something.

59:29.357 --> 59:30.441
That was almost bad.

59:35.446 --> 59:36.739
Do you have feelings for me?

59:42.161 --> 59:43.246
No. Why?

59:43.329 --> 59:44.789
It seems like you do.

59:46.583 --> 59:49.043
Well, I don't.

59:58.761 --> 01:00:00.138
Does it seem like it?

01:00:02.473 --> 01:00:05.435
You should know,
I don't just flirt around.

01:00:06.269 --> 01:00:08.396
No. I'm not just flirting.

01:00:08.479 --> 01:00:09.689
So let me date you.

01:00:09.772 --> 01:00:12.483
What? What happened
to let's not date just 'cause we…

01:00:12.567 --> 01:00:16.904
I wouldn't want to
if I were the only one with feelings.

01:00:22.910 --> 01:00:25.246
If we both feel something, we date.

01:00:25.830 --> 01:00:27.248
If not, we don't.

01:00:31.210 --> 01:00:32.629
So which is it?

01:00:35.089 --> 01:00:38.092
What are, uh… we?

01:01:22.095 --> 01:01:24.597
It's true that the recent
collision on the expressway happened

01:01:24.681 --> 01:01:27.141
because the visibility
was low from the fog.

01:01:27.225 --> 01:01:29.894
Why is our country behind
at implementing fog advisories?

01:01:30.520 --> 01:01:33.147
Reporters should have
enough integrity, not to twist facts.

01:01:33.231 --> 01:01:35.233
You have to be ready
if you do stuff like that.

01:01:35.316 --> 01:01:36.317
Ha-kyung's smart.

01:01:36.401 --> 01:01:39.529
There's a reason she's the youngest
director the division's ever had.

01:01:39.612 --> 01:01:40.822
- I think we need--
- Without a full plan?

01:01:40.905 --> 01:01:42.365
I think she works here.

01:01:42.448 --> 01:01:45.076
- If not, why would she hide?
- Thanks for this. You may go.

01:01:45.159 --> 01:01:48.079
What? She's messing with him, right?

01:01:48.162 --> 01:01:49.080
What? No, no! Hang up!

01:01:49.163 --> 01:01:50.039
Oh, Forecaster.

01:01:50.123 --> 01:01:52.417
You need to find cases
from other countries that have fogs

01:01:52.500 --> 01:01:54.085
like we do, I need them in the morning.

01:01:54.168 --> 01:01:55.294
What is all this?

01:01:55.378 --> 01:01:56.337
I stayed up for you.

01:01:57.380 --> 01:01:59.173
This office romance
will be the death of me.
